{"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Previews-Article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit preview engine."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI previews let you work on your project in Xcode without having to launch the app all the time. Just update your view and models, and the preview will automatically update."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit has preview-specific services and state that can be used in your previews. This makes it easy to preview keyboard-specific views directly in Xcode.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"👑 KeyboardKit Pro can unlock powerful keyboard preview components that can be added to the main app target, for instance to show the result of specific configurations and styles. You can sign up for KeyboardKit Pro from the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/keyboardkit.com","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"anchor":"Preview-specific-state--services","type":"heading","text":"Preview-specific state & services","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit adds preview-specific shorthand for all services and states, to make it easy to apply preview-specific values. For instance, consider that you want to preview this view:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct CustomView: View {","","    init(actionHandler: KeyboardActionHandler) {","        self.actionHandler = actionHandler","    }","","    private var actionHandler: KeyboardActionHandler","","    @EnvironmentObject private var context: KeyboardControllerContext","","